MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7022015696809122566}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1e36ebc0b8de90543a18645594dd9db3, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  note: "HitAnimSwitch component (Optional):\n\nAutomatically detected by HitController
    on Start. When EnableHits() called on Hit Controller to enable hits, it switches
    to given Animation State on given Animator with its duration. When hits disabled,
    it switches back to initial animation state. So it allows to play a supporting
    player animation while using hits. \n\nIn this case, it plays a Drums animation
    on the animator when starting to use a DrumKit interaction, and ends when finished
    using that InteractorObject."
--- !u!114 &7022015696809122573
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7022015696809122566}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1e36ebc0b8de90543a18645594dd9db3, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  note: 'HitController component:


    Handles hit animations for one hand pick up objects with configurable timing and
    trajectories. Animates transforms through hit sequences using bezier curves and
    triggers hit reactions on target characters. Each hit can be assigned a key with
    events. Set up hits in the inspector and call StartHitAnimation() or press assigned
    keys to execute.


    There is another HitController in children on DrumKitBodyHits for supporting body
    movements.'
--- !u!114 &7022015696809122574
